SELECT 'dumsor-water-internet-ghana-infrastructure-playbook', 'Dumsor, Dry Taps and 81% MTN: The Returnee Infrastructure Playbook', '<p>''Don''t come here expecting America. It''s not America.'' Every long-stay returnee lands on the same doctrine: <strong>you have to be your own infrastructure</strong>. Medical care is best with money, power with backup, water with storage, internet with redundancy. Here''s the full picture.</p><h2>Power: dumsor never fully left</h2><p>The 2012-16 crisis (12hrs on/24 off, ~$1B lost in 2014) eased, but ECG''s <strong>$1.7B+ supplier debt</strong>, plant shutdowns and grid fires keep 2024-26 flare-ups coming - plus prepaid meters reportedly draining 3x fast. Returnees report 14-hour cuts, spoiled fridge food, and AC bills of $100-150/month where they run cooling. <strong>Setup:</strong> solar + inverter as baseline, generator for heavy loads, housing chosen for existing backup, router UPS for short cuts, cowork spaces mapped for long ones.</p><h2>Water: bills without water</h2><p>Taps dry for months - even a year - while Ghana Water bills keep arriving; families survive on poly-tanks and trucked water. <strong>Setup:</strong> overhead tank + booster pump standard; borehole where viable; never rent without confirming flow history with neighbours, not the landlord.</p><h2>Internet: cheap per GB, pricey to live on</h2><p>MTN holds ~81% of mobile data; ~40% of your data spend is levies; 11-99 fibre cuts a day at $3,200 a repair keep quality uneven. Mandated bigger bundles didn''t lower entry prices. <strong>Setup:</strong> fibre home line + two mobile SIMs (MTN + Telecel), phone tethering ready, offline-first work habits.</p><h2>Roads price everything</h2><p>Good roads command premium rents; bad roads strand Ubers and ambulances alike. Flooding zones (Kasoa corridors, Weija downstream, Ramsar wetlands) destroy assets yearly - location diligence is infrastructure diligence.</p><p><em>Ask people living your target street how the lights, taps and mast behave - <a href=''/workspace.html''>find them on Sporafind</a> before you sign.</em></p>', '14-hour blackouts, water bills without water, duopoly internet, potholes that price rent. Why you must be your own utility - and the exact setup.', ARRAY['dumsor','infrastructure','utilities','internet','relocation'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-06T08:00:00.000Z', 'Ghana Infrastructure Playbook: Power, Water, Internet', 'Dumsor blackouts, dry taps, MTN-dominated internet, bad roads: the returnee setup - solar, tanks, dual-SIM, UPS - that makes Ghana work.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'dumsor-water-internet-ghana-infrastructure-playbook');
