SELECT 'ghana-healthcare-schools-diaspora-families-guide', 'Healthcare and Schools in Ghana: What Diaspora Families Must Know', '<p>Two decisions dominate family relocation: <strong>who treats us when we''re sick, and who teaches our kids</strong>. Ghana answers both - but on Ghanaian terms that punish the unprepared.</p><h2>Healthcare: two systems, one rule</h2><p>Public hospitals are affordable with long waits and uneven equipment; private facilities (Nyaho, Lister, UG Medical Centre) deliver near-Western standards at Western-adjacent prices - GHS 200-300 per consultation plus GHS 150-300 per prescription round, tests extra. Emergency response is the weak link: ambulances unreliable, so private ERs are the plan. The rule veterans repeat: <strong>come with insurance or a medical savings buffer</strong> - bills ''through the roof'' for severe needs.</p><h2>The NHIS gap</h2><p>Stark finding: <strong>75% of immigrants never enrolled</strong> in the NHIS versus 7.8% of locals - paper-based enrolment repels digital-first migrants. The 2026 Free Primary Healthcare policy covers preventive/basic care for all residents, but anything beyond still needs NHIS or private cover. <strong>Chronic conditions:</strong> confirm your exact medication is stocked locally before moving; carry surplus and a shipment plan.</p><h2>Schools: excellent, pricey, waitlisted</h2><p>GIS, SOS Hermann Gmeiner, TIS, DPS, Al Rayan, Lincoln Community: strong outcomes at <strong>GHS 8,000-50,000 per term</strong> with peak-season waitlists. Start admissions months early; budget a full year plus transport. The UK comparison flatters Ghana (£400/term vs £65/day) - but only if you secure the seat.</p><p><em>Moving with family? <a href=''/workspace.html''>Sporafind</a> finds diaspora parents at your shortlisted schools - real fee, real waitlist, real experience.</em></p>', 'Public vs private care, the 75% NHIS enrolment gap, chronic-meds planning, and international school fees of GHS 8-50K per term.', ARRAY['healthcare','schools','NHIS','family','relocation'], 'Relocation Guides', 'published', '2026-10-07T08:00:00.000Z', 'Ghana Healthcare & Schools Guide for Diaspora Families', 'NHIS vs private insurance, best private hospitals, chronic medication planning, and Accra international school costs for returning families.'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blog_posts WHERE slug = 'ghana-healthcare-schools-diaspora-families-guide');
